        <p>tieulars given as to the reasons for the aatic and eventually on being put to the meeting t resolution of censure was lost by an overwhel ing majority, only 1/ voting in favour of it. An assurance was asked for and given that the proposed cottages to be built, as far as was possible to do so, Warrington labour shot] be employed.</p>
