        <p>PADGATE.</p>
        <p>Wesley Guild.—The monthly devotional meet- ing was held on Monday evening, presided over by the Rev. E. Morgan. A thoughtful and in- teresting paper on "The optimism of love" was given by Miss Beckett. A duet rendered by Mrs. James Bennett and Miss Nicholson was much appreciated. The roll was called by Mr. Harold Tomlin, after which the various pledges were repeated .by the members.</p>
        <p>Wesleyan Church Meeting.—A church meet- ing was held in the Wesley Hall on Wednesday for the purpose of discussing the ways and means by which the necessary funds for the up- keep of the church might he increased. The Rev. E. Morgan presided. Miss Nicholson sang in her usual pleasing style "Caller Herrin'." At the close of the formal proceedings refresh- ments were handed round, after which there was a sale of work, the proceeds realising,- £l2.</p>
