      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-03-07_WidnesExaminer_art0195" n="art0195">
        <head>Other Churches Astonished.</head>
        <p>Other Churches Astonished.</p>
        <p>Then begau the descent, and the membership' began to go down. Why? There was a variety of reasons, but one was that the other churches were FO astonished at the results, ;that they looked round for something of the kind. Be believed he was right in saying there were no Bible-classes in any of the Anglican Churches. When these classes were formed the member- ship of their P.S.A. began to 'decline, hut he never found fault with that, because they could</p>
        <p>only do good, for it was a better thing when men would rally round their own church on a Sunday afternoon than when they went to an- other place. He was bound to say that people thought that the P.S.A. iihould be a factor in the constitution of Wycliffe Church.</p>
      </div>
