        <p>Attitude of Labour Representative on Education Committee Criticised.</p>
        <p>SCHOOL CARETAKERS' WAGES.</p>
        <p>Many items of interest to the workers were discussed at the monthly meeting of the War- rington Trades and Labour Council on Tuesday night, and perhaps the chief topics were those of Labour representation and the conditions of the school caretakers, and the attitude of the Labour representative on the Education Com- mittee was criticised. Mr. E. , Randells pre- sided.</p>
        <p>The Chairman said they were aware that at the present time several societies affiliated to the Council were having a dispute with Messrs. Fletcher, Russell, and it behoved the Council to give the strikers every assistance they could. It was to be hoped that the men came out vic- toriOus, and probably that Council would be asked to give them some backing. (Applause.)</p>
      </div>
