      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-03-07_WidnesExaminer_art0243" n="art0243">
        <p>vThe recent victory of Rylands' Recreation team over Abram Rangers adds further '!aurels to an already fine record established by the Gorsey-lane organisation. The win by 11 Paints to three secured for them the Lancashire lutlior Cup, an honour they almost achieved two years ago, when, after a hard game, they were defeated in the final by the Runcorn White •Vtar• So far this season their colours have not .Jeon lowered in a League game, and there is 1511117 prospect of their retaining the Manchester "441 District League Shield. The team has not 4et exigted five seasons, but has a remarkable or successes. 41.1. the first and second seasons they were '.,,,s'itkiated to the St. Helens and District League, they found it possible, at the first attempt, eaPture the League trophy. In th.. second</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-03-07_WidnesExaminer_art0244" n="art0244">
        <head>PROUD RECORD.</head>
        <p>A PROUD RECORD.</p>
        <p>year they worked their'way to the final, but the cup was snatched from their possession by the White Rose at St. Helens. The third year operations were in the Second Division of the Manchester League, and here our local team distinguished themselves by only receiving one defeat throughout the competition.. That year they were defeated in the final of the Lancashire Junior Cup, but were successful in obtaining the Manchester and District Shield, and the ' honours in the Warrington Works Competition. aFbi carriedlr First Performance all Divisionb efooi fe of flreg maManchester imakingn gaining Last year they threw in their lot with the pionship at the first time of asking. retained the season wofiththeonmlyatnwchoesdteefrtsLea, ag nu de through g commend- able eCmyhearnmadn: ti e Ltheea League, and</p>
      </div>
