        <p>Canada's Largest Province. The location of Quebec, combined with its stupendous resources, gives this Province unsur- passed advantages as a manufacturing and distribut- ing centre, and unique claims on the attention of investors. • QUEBEC HAS OVER 6,000 FACTORIES and mills producing pulp and paper, mining and other machinery, powder and fulminites, mechanical and structural iron works, woollen and worsted goods, cottons and prints; rubber and mechanical rubber goods, tobacco, cigars, canned meat, biscuits, &amp;c., &amp;c. CHEAP ELECTRIC POWER FOR MANUFACTURERS. The Water Powers of 20 million h.p.—hal that estimated Quebec can an develop forel'ehleenzr e Dominion. Manufacturers can rely on obtaining electricity in unlimited WHIM at the lowest rates. RICH MINERAL DEPOSITS. The undeveloped mineral resources of Quebec offer an inviting field to prospectors. In 1912 Quebec produced two million dollars worth more minerals than in any previous year, awl nine-tenths of the world's supply of asbestos. STRONG FINANCIAL POSITION. To unlimited internal resources the Province of Quebec adds financial stability, and a go-ahead and public-spirited Provincial Government. ATTRACTIONS FOR SPORTSMEN AND TOURISTS. No other Province offers such attractions to the .Sportsman deiV rin'°lotiorsi set,. ai'ill'(hc forests are richly stocked 'Caribou ; the rivers teem with salmon, trout, and ournaniehe ; the historic cities are full of interest; the scenery is delightful. For further particulars apply to Lieut.col, the Mini Pe PELLET IER AGENT-GENERAL FOR QUEBEC, 56, Atingsway, London W.C.</p>
