        <p>A Silk Season. "And ye shall walk in silk attire" is evidently Fashion's decree this year. Women can now be dressed entirely in this medium, for every ' item of a wardtobe, from hats to shoes, may be of. silk. Many of the transparent materials , composed of it are almost as fine and delicate as spiders' webs; and as for ribbons, there seems to le no limitation to their variety. Their designs, too, are marvellous in colour, ingenuity and taste. Gold is introduced to throw into relief the floral designs of the new taffetas, which are soft and rich. The newest crepes are beau- tifully hand-painted, but these are used chiefly by milliners. Shading, bright and brilliant, is a novelty in colour schemes, and plaids bid fair to remain in Savour throughout the coming summer—an exception to the general rule. The Nbw Corsets. Corsets are a very important itom of women's dress, and one to which, as a rule,, too little at- tention is paid. A new pair every ;season is not an extravagance, but a necessity, for the silhouette changes, and corsets naturally change with it. Nothing could be more hygienic than the new makes for this seal- designers have very wisely had recourse to science and to Nature, and the, result is most satisfactory. Time was when corsets were noth- ing more nor less than instruments of torture, in which the body was confined to the detriment of the wearer's health. All that has now been happily changedl. The new silhouette differs very slightly from that of last year, and it is rather in the materials employed than in the shape that changes aTe evident. Elastic is largely used now; in fact, some new models are made entirely of it. Stockingette, too, has taken the place of the stiff, unyielding mate- rials, that used to be considered indispensable to a good fitting corset. The Fashionable Waist. Yet the corsets of to_-day still afford support, whilst they permit of perfect freedom of move- ment. They are still cut very low, the upper part being merely a waist-belt of elastic. But Art.(r.'l4o.) Agal.vo</p>
